{% set local_problem %}
<p>Madison's mature tree coverage means gutters fill up fast. Pine needles accumulate year-round. Oak and maple leaves blanket everything in fall. And with 55+ inches of annual rainfall, clogged gutters don't just look bad — they actively damage your home.</p>

<p>When gutters overflow, water pours down your siding, pools around your foundation, and seeps into places it shouldn't. Madison's clay soil doesn't absorb that water — it just sits there, finding its way into your basement or crawlspace. Foundation repairs can cost $10,000-30,000. Regular gutter cleaning costs a fraction of that.</p>

<p>Many Madison homeowners try to clean gutters themselves, but it's time-consuming, uncomfortable, and potentially dangerous work. Our professional service is faster, more thorough, and safer — and we spot problems you might miss.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Our gutter cleaning service is comprehensive. We remove all debris by hand from inside your gutters — leaves, pine needles, roof grit, and anything else that's accumulated. We don't just blow debris onto your lawn or push it toward the downspouts.</p>

<p>Next, we flush all downspouts with water to ensure they're clear and flowing properly. Clogs in downspouts are a common problem that many homeowners miss when cleaning gutters themselves.</p>

<p>Finally, we inspect your entire gutter system for problems: loose hangers, small leaks, rust spots, and fascia damage. We'll let you know if we find anything that needs attention. When we're done, we clean up all debris — your property will look better than when we arrived.</p>
{% endset %}

